{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":1,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1509455328,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDU6SXNzdWUyNjk5NTE3MTE=","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1943","origin":"github"},"title":"Add option(s) to exclude/stub data during export based on meta-data","message":"Not sure if should be done as a part of #1928 and #1942 , probably not.\n\nMain use-case is to not export (by default) any file with (annex) metadata having `distribution-restrictions` set.\nOne way is to make it accept a dictionary (not sure how in command line) with meta-data fields and desired values regex to be excluded, so by default could then be `exclude_meta={'distribution_restrictions': '.*'}`\n\nAdditional option could be `exclude_method` with choices `stub` and `strip` (I like stub better for the default).  In case of `stub` (trickier I guess, but should be doable since we are instructing filename within archive anyways) we would need to replace those files with content `Content of the file was not included into the export. Contact original owner` or something like that.  Although while thinking about #1944 -- stripping is the easiest, since 'stub' would complicate bringing those files back into git-annex.","files":null}]}